<title>USA: NYSE says Wyle suspended after VEBA tender.</title>
<headline>NYSE says Wyle suspended after VEBA tender.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-08-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>The New York Stock Exchange said Wednesday that it is suspending trading in the common stock of Wyle Electronics effective immediately, and will ask the Securities and Exchange Commission to delist the issue.</p>
<p>The NYSE said it was taking the action because a tender offer by Raab Archer AG, a subsisdiary of VEBA AG, has left fewer than 600,000 Wyle shares outstanding.</p>
<p>The exchange said it is normal procedure to delist companies with fewer than 600,000 publicly held shares.</p>
